/target
**/*.rs.bk
node_modules/
dist/
.DS_Store
__pycache__/

# The gate's own capture file. `scripts/gate.sh > gate.log 2>&1` is what CONTRIBUTING.md tells a
# contributor to run for a multi-hour gate, and the summary now reports which files THIS RUN
# changed by comparing the tree before and after, so a tracked log would make every run
# report its own log.
gate.log

# Build output of the dependency-free Java verifier (issue #118); scripts/java-verify.sh
# creates and removes it, so it is never a source of truth.
sdks/java/out/

# Build output of the .NET verifier (issue #118); scripts/dotnet-verify.sh recreates it.
sdks/dotnet/**/bin/
sdks/dotnet/**/obj/

# Android sample build output (issue #116); scripts/mobile-verify.sh recreates it.
clients/mobile/android/app/build/
clients/mobile/android/.gradle/
clients/mobile/android/build/
clients/mobile/android/local.properties

# The MEASURED results the conformance page is generated from (issue #129). A RUN artifact,
# not a committed one: it carries the raw tenant, client, and user ids of whichever run
# produced it, so committing it would churn on every run and the drift check that keeps the
# page honest would be turned off within a week. The generated page IS the published
# artifact, and it is committed and drift-checked.
docs/conformance/mcp-results.json
